1. Clone the Repository
First, you need to clone the repository to your local machine:



git clone https://github.com/facebookresearch/demucs.git
cd demucs



Step 2: Create a Virtual Environment
Next, create a virtual environment to isolate your dependencies (recommended practice).

Run the following command to create a virtual environment using virtualenv:

pip3 install virtualenv


Then create a virtual environment in your project directory:

python3 -m venv venv

This will create a folder named venv where your virtual environment and its dependencies will be stored.


Step 3: Activate the Virtual Environment
Now, activate the virtual environment:

On macOS/Linux:

source venv/bin/activate


Step 4: Install Dependencies
Now that the virtual environment is activated, install the required dependencies listed in the requirements.txt file:

pip3 install -r requirements.txt




python3 -m demucs --mp3 --mp3-bitrate 320 -o "/Users/bhavin.barot/Documents/Python/Music Project/demucs/SourceAudio/Output" "/Users/bhavin.barot/Documents/Python/Music Project/demucs/SourceAudio/AapneYadKarva.mp3"







1. Standard Command to Separate Tracks
Since you want to separate audio tracks (e.g., vocals, drums, etc.), you can use the basic command as follows:



python3 -m demucs /Users/bhavin.barot/Documents/Python/Music\ Project/demucs/SourceAudio/Vasant\ rutu\ aavi.mp3


Note:

Make sure to quote file paths with spaces, like "Music Project" in your case.
Replace your_audio_file.mp3 with the actual audio file name you want to process.




2. If You Want MP3 Output
If you prefer the output in MP3 format, you can use the --mp3 flag and specify the bitrate (e.g., 192k, 320k):

python3 -m demucs --mp3 --mp3-bitrate 320 -o "/Users/bhavin.barot/Documents/Python/Music Project/demucs/Output" "/Users/bhavin.barot/Documents/Python/Music Project/demucs/SourceAudio/Darshan.mp3"





